course: dictionary
lesson: 15724
title: Transactions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A transaction is an act of buying, selling, paying or moving money. When you pay for a sandwich at the till, that is a transaction. «Mum made three transactions at the shop today.» Each time she paid, one transaction happened.
explain: Transactions can also be dealings between people. This is a more formal meaning. «The two friends made a fair transaction when they swapped their stickers.» Here the word means an exchange, where each person gives something and gets something back.
explain: Banks keep a list of transactions, so you can check where your money went. The words around a word give clues. If you see money, paid or card near the word, it is probably about buying or paying.
fact: A transaction is an act of buying, selling, paying or moving money.
fact: «Transactions» is the plural. One transaction, two or more transactions.
fact: Card payments, online payments and money moved between bank accounts are all transactions.
fact: In formal writing, a transaction can mean a dealing or exchange between people.
fact: Banks keep a list of transactions so you can check where your money went.
exercise: «Paying for a bag of crisps at the till was one transaction.» What is a transaction in this sentence? | A paper bag | *An act of paying money | A type of crisp | A shop window
exercise: Find the word for more than one transaction: «The bank list showed three transactions from Friday.» | transaction | Friday | *transactions | bank
exercise: «Jade paid for her shoes by card, and the transaction showed on her bank list.» Why is the bank list useful? | It holds the shoes | *It shows where money went | It shows the weather | It tells the time
test: «The two friends made a fair transaction, swapping stickers.» What does transaction mean here? | A type of card game | A dark cupboard | A sticker book | *A dealing or exchange between people
test: Which one is an online transaction? | Drawing a picture | Walking to school | Reading a library book | *Paying for a game download by card
exam: «Ella checked her bank list and saw one transaction she did not recognise.» What should Ella do? | Ignore it forever | Eat a sandwich | *Check it and tell the bank if it is wrong | Add the transaction to her homework
